WEBVTT

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:17.320
Yo, hurry up and help.

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:20.780
I'm going to have you pay for 
the inconvenience of having you

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.370
show up in the middle of the 
night, as well as for your stay.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:26.180
Making money first thing in the morning?

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.090
You still smell like the sewers.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.340
<i>Get your ass over here, Soleil, you lowlife.</i>

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.680
The number you have called is...

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.960
<i>Our community safety division's 
evidence storage was raided.</i>

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.080
<i>They took documents on fire dragons' 
and black dragons' heads.</i>

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:51.070
I see.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.740
<i>Since the evidence is now missing, 
I'm reducing your reward.</i>

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.880
<i>I spilled milk on my shirt this morning,</i>

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.820
<i>and my daughter ran away 
from home and I broke a plate,</i>

00:00:57.820 --> 00:01:00.600
<i>so I'm charging you for that, too.</i>

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.120
What kind of bullshit is that?

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:04.040
Sounds rough.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.400
I guess.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:08.290
That aside, do you know what this is?

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:10.140
What's this?

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.920
A shred of clothing from the witch
 we encountered last night.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.050
I've never seen such material.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.290
A specialist Jushikiist might know.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:20.090
Please.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.520
Make it quick if you can.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:22.720
Of course.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.870
I love actual Jushiki shop work.

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:28.020
This is a nice gem.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:32.220
Of course. It was made by 
the great gem craftsman,

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:34.570
Fleggun of late-age Damascus.

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.780
Its computational ability is enhanced 
with specialized equations,

00:01:37.780 --> 00:01:42.330
and the various Jushiki-disabling abilities 
that result are great for the front line.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.200
I see.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.220
Yo, wait.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:48.580
You're supposed to check with the accountant
first. That's the way the world works.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.000
We're perpetually broke.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:56.320
Why would we <i>ever</i> buy Jushiki 
gear that's worth an entire house?

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.340
Mine was getting old.

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.340
<i>Was</i>?

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:03.720
I've already signed a 
monthly installment contract.

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:05.750
Thank you.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:45.740
<b>Weaver of Light</b>

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.140
Coming!

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.450
You really do smell like the sewers.

00:03:53.450 --> 00:03:55.720
Better than perfume, isn't it?

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:58.750
I wouldn't let such a cheater into my home.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.120
You actually jumped into a sewer?

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:03.260
We had our reasons.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:04.910
All right, get undressed.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.490
The bath is ready.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:08.350
I'll take my pants off by myself.

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:11.270
Oh, come on.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:13.320
Miss Jivvy...

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:15.050
I really want to do you right now.

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:16.640
Not happening.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.680
You have work this afternoon.

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:19.850
It's fine.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.990
No.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:26.000
I understand your job is dangerous,

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.990
so I can't let it get any more dangerous.

00:04:30.760 --> 00:04:32.660
Honestly, your work...

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:37.600
Sorry I couldn't go to the Eridana 
Festival with you because of urgent work.

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:38.540
It's okay.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.700
Never mind that, Gayus...

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:44.130
You still smell like the sewers.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:52.350
<i>We have an update on the 
Serial Jushikiist Murders.</i>

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:55.150
<i>Today, on Wella Street in Eridana City,</i>

00:04:55.150 --> 00:05:00.520
<i>Jushiki engineer Lolorf Iscafendler 
was attacked with offensive Jushiki.</i>

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.030
<i>The suspect is still on the loose.</i>

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:08.490
<i>Gayus?</i>

00:05:08.490 --> 00:05:09.740
Hey, Vinnel.

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.740
<i>What do you want to know today?</i>

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:16.250
Find out about a woman named 
Nidvork or something like that.

00:05:16.250 --> 00:05:18.480
Black hair, green eyes.

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.710
A beautiful woman, either Alurian 
or from the eastern Seg region.

00:05:21.710 --> 00:05:27.230
She uses gravity Jushiki at an 
Enlightened or higher level.

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:30.970
Her husband is named Eningiluud.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:34.010
<i>That's plenty of information to...</i>

00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:35.480
<i>Hmm, she's not coming up.</i>

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:38.650
I tried looking her up, too, 
but there are no records.

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:41.230
<i>A lot of people, even in the Jushikiist Guild,</i>

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:44.490
<i>don't publicize their personal information.</i>

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:49.490
<i>We may have to hack into the guild or the 
government's data stores to find anything.</i>

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:52.620
That's why I'm asking you, information broker.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:54.900
<i>All right. I'll give it a try.</i>

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:04.570
Hey.

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:06.220
Oh, Gayus.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:08.570
Deep-fried pollock and 
deep-fried bread. Ten each.

00:06:08.570 --> 00:06:10.640
And some of today's specials.

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:13.100
That's quite an order.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:15.470
It's all for Gigina.

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:19.340
Front line Jushikiists eat like horses.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:22.890
Oh yeah, Arzel, you made 
a huge splash yesterday.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:24.500
You saw?

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:25.480
From a distance.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.400
Look, they used my photos and article.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:32.630
Although it's under my boss's name.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:36.620
"Tienlun Accord Resistance Movement.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:41.380
Participants insist that dragons 
and humans can never reconcile."

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.400
Read the whole thing.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:48.910
I wrote about how the pro-accord 
people believe it's the accord

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:51.510
that keeps an all-out war from happening.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:56.640
Are you in favor of the Seven-City 
Alliance ratifying the Tienlun Accord?

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:58.480
In principle.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.780
But I know how the critics feel, too.

00:07:01.350 --> 00:07:05.590
A lot of people have lost their families 
and loved ones to the dragons.

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:11.160
That aside, do you know anything 
about the Serial Jushikiist Murders?

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.400
Nope.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:15.000
You might be a target, too, you know.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.160
It's my time to shine, then.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:18.250
Ta-dah!

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:21.880
It's time for today's exciting 
Horton Fortune Telling.

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:24.380
It's time for you to end it. End it <i>all</i>.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:26.490
Bam!

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:29.000
Watch out for cars, glasses!

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:36.490
I just took some pictures by reflex,

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:38.580
but this isn't going to 
make for a good article.

00:07:46.770 --> 00:07:50.240
You have no trouble riding bikes,

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.320
but you're terrible with cars, Gigina.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.240
Bikes are like horses.

00:07:54.240 --> 00:07:56.140
But cars make no sense.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:07:57.600
They're the vehicle of demons.

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.150
Hurry up and get used 
to civilization already.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.460
Let's get this over with.

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:05.130
It's the last day of our 
pain-in-the-ass bodyguard duty.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:29.040
Thanks for coming so early in the morning.

00:08:29.040 --> 00:08:31.400
Or were we just late?

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:36.510
To think that Your Eminence would be 
thirty minutes late for an arrangement...

00:08:36.510 --> 00:08:38.240
Have you not heard

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:42.540
the Draken saying, "One cannot 
swing their blade without their head"?

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:46.790
I'm stealing Gigina's line here,
but it seems to be spot on.

00:08:47.320 --> 00:08:50.360
I'd like to imitate you, too, but I'm 
going to have to restrain myself,

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:55.090
seeing as this dog shit has put on 
a great performance on the streets.

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:57.580
That's some big talk for a Draken.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.760
You even have a picture diary.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.850
And I know you use "boku" for 
your first-person pronoun.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:03.950
You!

00:09:03.950 --> 00:09:06.280
How did you unlock the office cabinet?

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:11.680
It's not hard to open with the technique 
that our old bounty taught us before.

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:15.660
Well, I know that you said you choose 
your lewd image storage devices

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:19.660
more carefully than you'd choose your wife.

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:22.640
How did you hear that?!

00:09:22.640 --> 00:09:26.670
I was doing repairs inside the dresser 
when I heard you muttering to yourself.

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.380
You furniture freak!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.490
Go get swallowed by a man-eating chair!

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:34.090
I might want a chair like that.

00:09:34.580 --> 00:09:35.620
Jeez...

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:38.590
This is some excellent 
early morning entertainment.

00:09:39.190 --> 00:09:43.600
Watching you two might even
 be more fun than sightseeing.

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:49.660
Gayus Levina Soleil and Gigina 
Jardi Doruk Meleios Ashley-Bufh.

00:09:49.660 --> 00:09:53.980
We're just guards. I'm surprised 
you remembered our names.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:59.620
Remembering names is the least I can do 
for the people I become involved with.

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:06.540
So, where does His Eminence 
the Cardinal wish to see today?

00:10:07.250 --> 00:10:12.920
Right, I've made plans to have tea with a
guest from afar first thing today.

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:16.940
I expect it'll be quite 
a stimulating tea party.

00:10:33.380 --> 00:10:35.570
Do you not believe in God?

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:38.950
I can't really say,

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:44.450
but seeing the state of the world, 
I don't want to believe He physically exists.

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:49.180
I won't tell you that those are 
blasphemous words to utter

00:10:49.180 --> 00:10:52.740
in front of the guardian of the religion.

00:10:54.020 --> 00:10:56.320
Helodel's fiancée, Shifaka, died

00:10:56.320 --> 00:11:00.590
because of a silly dispute between the 
Dragon Empire and the Seven-City Alliance.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:03.280
If gods do exist,

00:11:03.280 --> 00:11:07.850
why do they allow people to be killed 
by wars, disease, or accidents?

00:11:08.360 --> 00:11:12.170
Why did my sister, Aleciel, have to die?

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:14.940
Is it wrong to ask for the reason?

00:11:17.000 --> 00:11:18.300
Very well.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:23.820
God either does not exist or is merciless.

00:11:25.290 --> 00:11:27.860
But how could we live without deception?

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:30.910
The dead do not come back to life.

00:11:30.910 --> 00:11:32.830
Miracles don't exist.

00:11:33.230 --> 00:11:36.910
Our world has no real purpose or meaning.

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:40.700
That's why people have no 
option but to close their eyes

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.840
and pretend in order to keep living.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:46.220
You ought to be careful about 
searching too hard for reasons.

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:51.500
You, well... All Jushikiists are 
attempting to understand this world.

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.460
But <i>that</i> is arrogance.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:57.390
We can't touch the world directly.

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:59.740
What are you...

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:03.290
That's my answer.

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.660
You'll have to come up with your own.

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.080
And pose a question.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.980
To face a question without an answer

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:15.670
is the only way we humans can fight reality.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:19.680
And of the many paths a human can take,

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:21.430
it is the most sincere and most venerable.

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:26.660
Are we done with the word games?

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:32.230
Appearances aside, 
you two get along quite well.

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:35.210
The only reason I work with him

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:38.230
is because if you ignore the fact that he's stupid,
obsessed with fighting and furniture,

00:12:38.230 --> 00:12:41.230
and has no sense of personal
financial responsibility,

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:43.280
he's a good partner.

00:12:43.710 --> 00:12:45.760
You two are complementary.

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:49.160
Your inability to accept 
things for what they are

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:52.360
must be your limit.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:56.300
The guest has arrived.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:08.880
Your Eminence, I look forward 
to our meeting today.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:09.930
Likewise.

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:11.390
Now, right this way.

00:13:46.420 --> 00:13:51.600
I <i>really</i> don't want to hear, 
but what's your idea of a good chair?

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.240
What else?

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:57.480
It has to ooze the quintessence
 of a chair. Noble, beautiful...

00:13:58.000 --> 00:14:00.160
Perhaps the pews here 
are of a good lineage.

00:14:00.160 --> 00:14:03.360
They're pious and have regal expressions.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:07.110
Anyway, Gayus, have you noticed?

00:14:07.110 --> 00:14:12.280
The guest is Representative Azu Bita 
of the Lapetodes Seven-City Alliance.

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.790
I know.

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:15.390
Representative Azu Bita is one of

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:19.040
the right-hand men of the Seven-City 
Alliance House's Supreme Chairman Kai Kuyou,

00:14:19.040 --> 00:14:21.130
and the executive of the 
Democratic Liberal Party.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:23.300
Why didn't you speak up, if you knew?

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:25.740
"Don't go near danger."

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:27.800
"Pretend you didn't see anything."

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:28.970
That was my dad's...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.020
Gigina!

00:14:59.200 --> 00:15:00.290
Those guys...

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.010
Gigina!

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:10.220
Yeah!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:35.820
Run!

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:40.910
I'll take it from here.

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:42.120
That'd be great.

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:43.540
What just happened?

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:46.540
We've got the opposite 
of allies on our hands!

00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:52.550
All the other guards are dead.

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.130
Prepare for evacuation.

00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:56.240
How are we supposed to get out of here?

00:15:56.240 --> 00:16:00.310
It's insane that a church that deals with
royalty doesn't have escape routes.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:05.860
We've taken care of a few assassins, 
but there must be more enemies.

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:08.510
If Gigina and I can stop them, we will.

00:16:08.510 --> 00:16:10.610
If not, we can at least buy time.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.860
Our lives are expendable.

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.090
But if you were to die,

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:19.870
there would be a war between the 
Dragon Empire and the Seven-City Alliance.

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:22.900
If that were to happen, we'd see 
that same tragedy happen again.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:25.800
I suspect you're right.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:28.760
And I'd like to show my respect to 
those who speak on their own lives

00:16:28.760 --> 00:16:32.760
more than to those who speak 
on the lives of others.

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:37.430
There's something I want 
more than respect or medals.

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:41.680
If I make it out of here alive,
 I would consider no reward too great.

00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.140
Then the truth, please.

00:16:45.780 --> 00:16:47.650
As much as you'd like.

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:54.570
They're coming.

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:02.500
Relish now the banquet of battle!

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:09.880
The blades of two lives meet, sending sparks.

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:13.720
Just for that moment, 
the world and I pulsate.

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:19.300
Now, show me your lives and your limits!

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:46.650
That about does it.

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:02.440
I'm impressed that an assassin exists

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:05.190
who can fight squarely 
against a Draken warrior.

00:18:05.860 --> 00:18:08.020
Leave me with your name before you die.

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:12.730
I can't do that, but I can tell you that I'm 
just a ninja who takes care of the Kouga clan.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:19.120
What the hell is that?

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:22.560
Third-order chemical alchemy Jushiki.

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:23.580
Chilliat.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.710
She generates hundreds of millions of
monomolecular needles, hurling them at her enemy.

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:31.330
She can pierce through just about anything.

00:18:31.330 --> 00:18:32.960
I can see that.

00:19:04.230 --> 00:19:08.580
The Kouga always finish their mission!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.380
Gigina!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:44.310
Aleciel! Aleciel!

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:21.950
<i>If only I'd died, too...</i>

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:24.470
<i>This is how it's supposed to be.</i>

00:20:26.280 --> 00:20:27.240
Please, no!

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.270
Please, no!

00:20:47.910 --> 00:20:49.210
Hello.

00:20:50.200 --> 00:20:52.100
H-Hello.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:55.770
Is this a hospital?

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:57.840
Yes.

00:20:57.840 --> 00:21:00.480
This is Eridana Private Hospital.

00:21:01.760 --> 00:21:04.870
This is like a foreign language
textbook conversation.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:13.520
Gayus came back to life!

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:15.680
That hurts...

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:16.870
Thank goodness.

00:21:17.240 --> 00:21:19.780
Thank goodness.

00:21:39.780 --> 00:21:44.660
It seems that such a powerful spell 
is difficult to endure, even for me.

00:21:50.330 --> 00:21:53.350
Am I mistaken, feline?

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:03.530
You don't fear me, do you?

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:14.040
My dear, I will avenge you with these hands.

00:23:50.720 --> 00:23:55.660
There are things far more terrifying 
than artful, ferocious malice.

00:23:56.150 --> 00:24:00.200
Nothing is more problematic than benevolence 
that is sincere to the point of foolishness.

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:04.580
Nobody can stop a disaster 
caused by good will.

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:04.920
<b>Ballet of the Winged</b>
